---
id: deferred-hydration
title: Deferred Hydration
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred hydration is experimental"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On an initial page load, TanStack Start server-renders your page so the browser\ncan show useful HTML quickly. Hydration is the client-side work that turns that\ninitial HTML document into an interactive app. It loads and executes JavaScript,\nruns components, attaches event handlers, and reconnects the existing DOM to\nReact."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred hydration applies to this initial document hydration work. After the\napp is already running, subsequent client-side navigations render through the\nclient app; there is no initial server HTML for TanStack Start to preserve."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, TanStack Start hydrates the full document. That is usually the\nsimplest and safest behavior, but large pages can spend meaningful startup time\nloading JavaScript and hydrating parts of the page that the user may not need\nright away."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred hydration lets you mark selected parts of a page as \"not interactive\nyet\". The server HTML remains in the document, but TanStack Start waits to\nhydrate that boundary until a strategy says it is time. By default, the compiler\nalso moves the boundary children into a separate JavaScript chunk so the browser\ncan delay loading that code too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use deferred hydration when a part of the page should be visible, styled, and\nindexable immediately, but does not need to be interactive immediately."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"add-a-deferred-boundary","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add A Deferred Boundary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" with a strategy from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-start/hydration"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '400px' })}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the initial server response, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reviews"},{"type":"text","value":" is still rendered to HTML. During the\ninitial client hydration pass, that HTML is preserved but the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reviews"},{"type":"text","value":" React\ntree does not hydrate yet. When the boundary comes within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"400px"},{"type":"text","value":" of the\nviewport, TanStack Start loads the deferred child chunk and hydrates the\nboundary."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" only preserves server HTML that exists in the initial document. If the\nsame boundary first mounts later, for example after client-side navigation,\nthere is no server HTML to preserve, so it renders normally on the client."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-what-to-defer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose What To Defer"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The right boundary depends on your page, your product priorities, and real user\nbehavior. TanStack Start cannot know which parts of your page are safe to delay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Good candidates are usually SSR content that is not needed for immediate\ninteraction:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Below-the-fold reviews, comments, product details, related content, or long\nmarketing sections."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rich widgets such as maps, charts, carousels, video players, editors, or\nembeds."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Panels that are activated by intent, such as filters, preview panes, or\ncontextual tools."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"UI that only matters for a matching media query."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static server-rendered content that should not hydrate on the initial\ndocument."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Poor candidates are parts of the page users may need immediately:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary navigation, route chrome, search boxes, and account controls."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Above-the-fold forms, add-to-cart buttons, checkout actions, or consent\ncontrols."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The interactive part of the LCP or hero area when users may click it\nimmediately."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessibility-critical controls that must be keyboard-ready as soon as the\npage appears."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components whose props, context, or shared state are expected to update\nimmediately after app startup."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Measure each boundary. A useful boundary reduces startup JavaScript or hydration\nwork without making expected interactions feel late."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"comparison-to-astro-islands","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison To Astro Islands"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Astro starts static and asks \"what should come alive?\" Each answer is an\nisolated framework root dropped into HTML. Islands are independent runtimes\nsharing a DOM."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start starts fully interactive and asks \"what can wait?\" The whole\ndocument hydrates as one Solid tree by default; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" boundaries are gates\ninside that tree. Context, state, and events flow through normally, and\nhydration is parent-first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same trigger vocabulary, different substrate: Astro composes runtimes, Start\nschedules one. That is why Start gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition()"},{"type":"text","value":", and intent\nbubbling, and why Astro gets multi-framework."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"comparison-to-solid-streaming-hydration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison To Solid Streaming Hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React's selective hydration controls the order in which server-rendered\nboundaries hydrate. Deferred hydration controls whether and when each\nboundary hydrates at all."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When React hydrates a streaming SSR page, every server-rendered\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Suspense>"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary will eventually hydrate. Selective hydration just\ndecides the order: each boundary hydrates as soon as its code arrives,\nand React jumps a boundary to the front of the queue if the user clicks\ninside it. The work is fixed by what the server rendered; React\nschedules it to feel responsive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred hydration changes what is in the queue in the first place. A\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary names a condition — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle()"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" — and the\nboundary stays as static server HTML until that condition fires. By\ndefault the child JavaScript also moves into a separate chunk that the\nbrowser does not download until the boundary is about to hydrate. If the\ncondition never fires, the boundary never hydrates and its code is never\nfetched."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two compose. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary decides whether and when React\nstarts hydrating a subtree; once it opens, anything inside it (including\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Suspense>"},{"type":"text","value":" boundaries) flows back into React's normal hydration\nscheduler. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Suspense>"},{"type":"text","value":" when hydration must happen and you want React\nto prioritize it well. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" when hydration might not need to\nhappen at all."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-three-decisions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Three Decisions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary has three performance decisions:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it controls"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydration"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the preserved server HTML becomes interactive."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code split"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether the children move into a generated deferred child chunk."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preparation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether work starts before the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" strategy hydrates the child."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"when-decide-when-the-boundary-hydrates","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":": decide when the boundary hydrates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" is required. Pass a strategy object for the common case:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate when={visible()}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a function when the decision needs browser-only information:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function RecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={() =>\n        navigator.connection?.saveData\n          ? interaction({ events: 'click' })\n          : visible()\n      }\n    >\n      <Recommendations />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function form is evaluated only on the client and must synchronously return\na strategy. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" when you intentionally want the initial server HTML to\nstay static."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"split-decide-whether-to-create-a-separate-child-chunk","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split"},{"type":"text","value":": decide whether to create a separate child chunk"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" splits the children into a generated child chunk:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate when={visible()}>\n  <HeavyWidget />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This delays both hydration work and child JavaScript loading."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":" when the child code is small or already needed elsewhere,\nand you only want to delay hydration work:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function SmallWidgetBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()} split={false}>\n      <SmallWidget />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"prefetch-decide-whether-to-start-loading-before-hydration","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":": decide whether to start loading before hydration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":" starts loading before the boundary hydrates. It has two forms:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use it for"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefetch strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch={idle()}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preloading the generated child chunk before hydration."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Procedural prefetch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch={async (ctx) => { ... }}"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preloading the child chunk plus data or other async resources."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both forms start work early, but they do not change when the boundary becomes\ninteractive. That is still controlled by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A prefetch strategy is the small, declarative form:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { idle, interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction()} prefetch={idle()}>\n  <ProductRecommendations />\n</Hydrate>\n\n<Hydrate\n  when={interaction()}\n  prefetch={visible({ rootMargin: '1200px' })}\n>\n  <RelatedProducts />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy-form "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":" downloads the generated child chunk before the boundary\nhydrates. This can make the later hydration trigger feel faster, because the\nbrowser may already have the chunk by the time "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves. Generated child\nchunks only exist when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split"},{"type":"text","value":" is enabled, so TypeScript rejects strategy-form\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":" when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use procedural prefetch when you need custom work:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { noop, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nfunction DeferredReviews() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={visible()}\n      prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n        await Promise.all([\n          preload(),\n          queryClient.query(reviewsQueryOptions).catch(noop),\n        ])\n      }}\n    >\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Procedural prefetch also works with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":". In that case, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nis a resolved no-op, but the function can still prepare data or other\nresources."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-recipes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common Recipes"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hydrate-below-the-fold-ssr-content","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrate below-the-fold SSR content"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ProductHero />\n      <BuyBox />\n\n      <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '800px' })}>\n        <Reviews />\n      </Hydrate>\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a positive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rootMargin"},{"type":"text","value":" when the boundary should hydrate before it actually\nenters the viewport."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"download-the-child-chunk-before-it-is-needed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download the child chunk before it is needed"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ReviewsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '200px' })} prefetch={idle()}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This keeps the boundary non-interactive until it is close to the viewport, but\nstarts loading the child chunk during idle time."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keep-a-widget-cold-until-user-intent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep a widget cold until user intent"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function RecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}\n      prefetch={visible({ rootMargin: '1200px' })}\n    >\n      <RecommendationCarousel />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is useful for expensive controls that are visible or nearby, but only\nmatter when the user reaches for them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"delay-hydration-without-code-splitting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Delay hydration without code splitting"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function BadgeBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()} split={false}>\n      <SmallPersonalizedBadge />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this when the JavaScript is already part of the startup bundle or when a\nseparate child chunk would not be worth it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keep-initial-ssr-html-static","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep initial SSR HTML static"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { never } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function MarketingPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={never()}>\n      <StaticTrustBadges />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" preserves the existing server HTML and does not hydrate the boundary\nduring initial document hydration. If the same boundary mounts later during\nclient-side navigation, it renders normally because there is no initial server\nHTML to preserve. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be used as a prefetch strategy."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reuse-hydrate-props","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reuse Hydrate props"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrateOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" for reusable objects that you spread into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport type { HydrateOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nconst belowFoldProps = {\n  when: () => visible({ rootMargin: '800px' }),\n} satisfies HydrateOptions\n\nexport function Page() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      {...belowFoldProps}\n      prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n        await preload()\n      }}\n    >\n      <Widget />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":" functions are supported. You do not need to wrap\nthem in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCallback"},{"type":"text","value":"; TanStack Start keeps the latest callback internally and\ndoes not re-register hydration listeners just because a function identity\nchanged. If the meaning of a boundary changes, use a normal React "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" to\ncreate a new boundary."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"hydrate-props-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrate Props Reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts these props:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prop"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrationStrategy | () => HydrationStrategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required. Controls when the boundary hydrates. Function form is client-only and synchronous."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrationPrefetchStrategy | HydrationPrefetchFunction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional. Strategy form preloads the split child chunk. Function form can preload chunks, data, or other resources, and can be used with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". Set literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable compiler extraction and only defer hydration work."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSX.Element"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-only loading UI for boundaries that mount after the app has already hydrated and then suspend on the child chunk or child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Suspense"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onHydrated"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fires once after the boundary has hydrated on the client."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"strategy-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy Reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import strategies from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-start/hydration"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates as soon as the app hydrates."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requestIdleCallback"},{"type":"text","value":", or after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"timeout"},{"type":"text","value":" when idle callbacks are unavailable."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates when the boundary marker enters the viewport."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates when the media query matches."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates on configured interaction intent events."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hydrates once the condition is truthy."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Never hydrates the initial server-rendered boundary."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy options:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ timeout?: number }"},{"type":"text","value":", defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2000"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ rootMargin?: string; threshold?: number | Array<number> }"},{"type":"text","value":", default margin "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"600px"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query string, for example "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media('(min-width: 800px)')"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ events?: supported event or readonly array of supported events }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Boolean or boolean-returning function."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported interaction events are "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auxclick"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"click"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contextmenu"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dblclick"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusin"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keydown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyup"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mousedown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mouseenter"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mouseover"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mouseup"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerdown"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerenter"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerover"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerup"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interaction()"},{"type":"text","value":" event list is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerenter"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusin"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointerdown"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"click"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"events"},{"type":"text","value":" when a boundary should listen to a\ndifferent event or a smaller set:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'dblclick' })}>\n  <PreviewEditor />\n</Hydrate>\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['contextmenu', 'dblclick'] })}>\n  <ContextMenuEditor />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition()"},{"type":"text","value":" boundary hydrates, it stays hydrated even if the condition\nlater becomes false:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { condition } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function CartRecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={condition(isCartOpen)}>\n      <CartRecommendations />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prefetch-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefetch Reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Procedural prefetch receives a context object:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Loads the compiler-generated child chunk. It resolves immediately when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitFor(strategy)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Waits for a prefetch strategy, the hydration trigger, or abort."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" for cancelable async work such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"element"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Boundary marker element for custom observers or DOM measurements."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitFor(strategy)"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves with:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'prefetch'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The supplied prefetch strategy resolved normally."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'hydrate'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The boundary's hydration trigger fired first. Do required work now."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'abort'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The boundary unmounted or the prefetch lifecycle was abandoned."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The promise returned from procedural prefetch is meaningful. Awaited work blocks\nhydration if the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" strategy resolves before the prefetch function\nfinishes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate\n  when={visible()}\n  prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n    await preload()\n  }}\n>\n  <Widget />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fire-and-forget work does not block hydration:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate\n  when={visible()}\n  prefetch={({ preload }) => {\n    void preload()\n  }}\n>\n  <Widget />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this distinction deliberately. Await when the resource is required for the\nfirst hydrated render. Fire and forget when the resource is only a helpful\nhead start."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"fallbacks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fallbacks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is not the placeholder for the initial server-rendered HTML. On the\ninitial page load, TanStack Start keeps the existing server HTML in place until\nthe boundary hydrates:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate when={visible()} fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In that example, if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Reviews"},{"type":"text","value":" was present in the initial HTML document, users\nsee the server-rendered reviews. They do not see "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReviewsSkeleton"},{"type":"text","value":" while the\nboundary is waiting for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is used when the boundary first appears after the app is already\nrunning and there is no existing server HTML for that boundary. Common examples\ninclude client-side navigation, conditionally showing a panel, or opening a tab\nwhose contents were not in the initial document. In those cases, the boundary\nrenders on the client, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" can show while the generated child chunk\nor a child "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Suspense"},{"type":"text","value":" is still loading."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":", initial server HTML remains static and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is not used."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler removes statically visible "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" props from the server bundle.\nPrefer passing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" directly, in an inline object spread, or through a\nsingle-use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const"},{"type":"text","value":" object spread so server builds can strip that UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"correctness-and-updates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Correctness And Updates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred hydration is a performance hint for React's initial hydration work.\nReact may hydrate a deferred boundary earlier than its strategy would normally\nallow if state, props, context, or store updates outside the boundary require\nReact to reconcile inside it before the gate opens. This preserves correctness\nand avoids showing stale server HTML after the surrounding app has changed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" is the exception for initial document hydration. Treat it as\nintentionally static SSR HTML. Do not rely on parent updates to make a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nboundary interactive. If the same boundary mounts later during client-side\nnavigation, it renders normally."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"nested-boundaries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nested Boundaries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nested boundaries hydrate parent-first. A child boundary can only hydrate after\nits ancestor boundaries have hydrated. That means non-interaction child\nstrategies such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"visible"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"media"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"condition"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot run while\ntheir parent boundary is still dehydrated."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, a product page might defer the whole reviews section until it is\nnear the viewport, while keeping heavier review tools cold until the user\ninteracts with them:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ProductHero />\n      <BuyBox />\n\n      <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '600px' })}>\n        <section aria-labelledby=\"reviews-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"reviews-heading\">Reviews</h2>\n          <ReviewsSummary />\n          <ReviewsList />\n\n          <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}>\n            <ReviewFilters />\n          </Hydrate>\n\n          <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'click' })}>\n            <WriteReviewForm />\n          </Hydrate>\n        </section>\n      </Hydrate>\n    </>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this example, scrolling near the reviews hydrates the parent first. Only\nafter that can the nested interaction boundaries hydrate from focus or click."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interaction intent can also resolve an unresolved ancestor chain when the\nancestor is itself waiting for interaction:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}>\n  <section aria-label=\"Review tools\">\n    <ReviewSortSummary />\n\n    <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'click' })}>\n      <WriteReviewForm />\n    </Hydrate>\n  </section>\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the first meaningful intent is a click inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WriteReviewForm"},{"type":"text","value":", TanStack\nStart hydrates the unresolved parent chain and then redispatches a same-type\nevent for the target boundary. Native listener payload details such as pointer\ncoordinates are not guaranteed to be preserved. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" ancestor still wins\nduring initial hydration, so descendants under it remain non-interactive."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"preloading-and-css","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preloading And CSS"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transformed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" JavaScript chunks are not modulepreloaded with the route.\nWithout "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":", the child chunk loads when the split boundary is ready to\nrender. If that import suspends during client-side navigation or another\nclient-only mount, the boundary's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" is shown."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSS used by split, deferred, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"never()"},{"type":"text","value":" boundaries is linked in the SSR HTML\nfor the matched route. It is not deferred with the generated child JavaScript\nchunk, because the server-rendered HTML may need those styles before any\nJavaScript runs. This is route-level asset linking: if a route module contains a\ndeferred boundary that imports CSS, that stylesheet can be linked for the route\neven when that boundary is hidden behind conditional rendering and does not\nappear in a particular response."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"extraction-limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extraction Limits"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiler-backed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" splitting works by moving the boundary's children into\na generated virtual module and rendering them through a lazy component. That\ngives TanStack Start a separate child chunk to load later, but it also means the\ncompiler must be able to move the JSX safely."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the component you want to split directly inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":". If you hide it\nbehind opaque "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" props, the compiler cannot statically extract those\nchildren into a generated child chunk at the usage site."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The split boundary must use a statically imported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" component from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-start"},{"type":"text","value":". Renaming that import is supported:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate as Deferred } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Deferred when={visible()}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Deferred>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assigning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" to another component variable is not analyzed for splitting:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\nconst Deferred = Hydrate\n\n<Deferred when={visible()}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Deferred>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render the imported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" tag directly, use an import rename, or set\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":" when you need component indirection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the literal prop "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":" to opt out of extraction. Dynamic values\nsuch as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={shouldSplit}"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be used to opt out at compile time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These patterns cannot be split:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pattern"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why it is rejected"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What to do instead"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function-as-children"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler cannot move a render function and preserve the expected call pattern."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":" or move the rendered UI into a child component."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render-time "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"use*"},{"type":"text","value":" calls directly inside extracted JSX"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving that JSX would move where the call executes."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move the call into a component inside the boundary, then render that component."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":" captures"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extracted function components cannot safely preserve class instance context."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap the UI in a function component or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"super"},{"type":"text","value":" captures"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extracted function components cannot preserve superclass access."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap the UI in a function component or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"split={false}"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This fails because "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useThing()"},{"type":"text","value":" would be moved into the generated component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<Hydrate when={idle()}>\n  <p>{useThing()}</p>\n</Hydrate>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move the call into a component instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ThingText() {\n  const thing = useThing()\n  return <p>{thing}</p>\n}\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()}>\n      <ThingText />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values captured from the surrounding component can be passed into the generated\nchild component, but keep the boundary simple. If extraction starts forcing\ncomplicated data flow, prefer a named child component and put the logic there."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fallback"},{"type":"text","value":" stripping is intentionally conservative. The server build can strip\ndirectly passed fallback UI, inline object-spread fallback UI, and single-use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"const"},{"type":"text","value":" object-spread fallback UI. If fallback props are hidden behind dynamic\nspreads or shared objects, the compiler may keep them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can extract reusable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefetch"},{"type":"text","value":" helpers today, but avoid hiding\nsplit boundaries behind plain wrapper components if you need child code\nsplitting. A wrapper can defer hydration at runtime, but the compiler cannot\nreliably move call-site children into a separate chunk through arbitrary\ncomponent indirection."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"add-a-deferred-boundary","text":"Add A Deferred Boundary","level":2},{"id":"choose-what-to-defer","text":"Choose What To Defer","level":2},{"id":"comparison-to-astro-islands","text":"Comparison To Astro Islands","level":2},{"id":"comparison-to-solid-streaming-hydration","text":"Comparison To Solid Streaming Hydration","level":2},{"id":"the-three-decisions","text":"The Three Decisions","level":2},{"id":"when-decide-when-the-boundary-hydrates","text":"when: decide when the boundary hydrates","level":3},{"id":"split-decide-whether-to-create-a-separate-child-chunk","text":"split: decide whether to create a separate child chunk","level":3},{"id":"prefetch-decide-whether-to-start-loading-before-hydration","text":"prefetch: decide whether to start loading before hydration","level":3},{"id":"common-recipes","text":"Common Recipes","level":2},{"id":"hydrate-below-the-fold-ssr-content","text":"Hydrate below-the-fold SSR content","level":3},{"id":"download-the-child-chunk-before-it-is-needed","text":"Download the child chunk before it is needed","level":3},{"id":"keep-a-widget-cold-until-user-intent","text":"Keep a widget cold until user intent","level":3},{"id":"delay-hydration-without-code-splitting","text":"Delay hydration without code splitting","level":3},{"id":"keep-initial-ssr-html-static","text":"Keep initial SSR HTML static","level":3},{"id":"reuse-hydrate-props","text":"Reuse Hydrate props","level":3},{"id":"hydrate-props-reference","text":"Hydrate Props Reference","level":2},{"id":"strategy-reference","text":"Strategy Reference","level":2},{"id":"prefetch-reference","text":"Prefetch Reference","level":2},{"id":"fallbacks","text":"Fallbacks","level":2},{"id":"correctness-and-updates","text":"Correctness And Updates","level":2},{"id":"nested-boundaries","text":"Nested Boundaries","level":2},{"id":"preloading-and-css","text":"Preloading And CSS","level":2},{"id":"extraction-limits","text":"Extraction Limits","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> Deferred hydration is experimental\n\nOn an initial page load, TanStack Start server-renders your page so the browser\ncan show useful HTML quickly. Hydration is the client-side work that turns that\ninitial HTML document into an interactive app. It loads and executes JavaScript,\nruns components, attaches event handlers, and reconnects the existing DOM to\nReact.\n\nDeferred hydration applies to this initial document hydration work. After the\napp is already running, subsequent client-side navigations render through the\nclient app; there is no initial server HTML for TanStack Start to preserve.\n\nBy default, TanStack Start hydrates the full document. That is usually the\nsimplest and safest behavior, but large pages can spend meaningful startup time\nloading JavaScript and hydrating parts of the page that the user may not need\nright away.\n\nDeferred hydration lets you mark selected parts of a page as \"not interactive\nyet\". The server HTML remains in the document, but TanStack Start waits to\nhydrate that boundary until a strategy says it is time. By default, the compiler\nalso moves the boundary children into a separate JavaScript chunk so the browser\ncan delay loading that code too.\n\nUse deferred hydration when a part of the page should be visible, styled, and\nindexable immediately, but does not need to be interactive immediately.\n\n## Add A Deferred Boundary\n\nUse `Hydrate` with a strategy from `@tanstack/solid-start/hydration`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '400px' })}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nOn the initial server response, `Reviews` is still rendered to HTML. During the\ninitial client hydration pass, that HTML is preserved but the `Reviews` React\ntree does not hydrate yet. When the boundary comes within `400px` of the\nviewport, TanStack Start loads the deferred child chunk and hydrates the\nboundary.\n\n`Hydrate` only preserves server HTML that exists in the initial document. If the\nsame boundary first mounts later, for example after client-side navigation,\nthere is no server HTML to preserve, so it renders normally on the client.\n\n## Choose What To Defer\n\nThe right boundary depends on your page, your product priorities, and real user\nbehavior. TanStack Start cannot know which parts of your page are safe to delay.\n\nGood candidates are usually SSR content that is not needed for immediate\ninteraction:\n\n- Below-the-fold reviews, comments, product details, related content, or long\n  marketing sections.\n- Rich widgets such as maps, charts, carousels, video players, editors, or\n  embeds.\n- Panels that are activated by intent, such as filters, preview panes, or\n  contextual tools.\n- UI that only matters for a matching media query.\n- Static server-rendered content that should not hydrate on the initial\n  document.\n\nPoor candidates are parts of the page users may need immediately:\n\n- Primary navigation, route chrome, search boxes, and account controls.\n- Above-the-fold forms, add-to-cart buttons, checkout actions, or consent\n  controls.\n- The interactive part of the LCP or hero area when users may click it\n  immediately.\n- Accessibility-critical controls that must be keyboard-ready as soon as the\n  page appears.\n- Components whose props, context, or shared state are expected to update\n  immediately after app startup.\n\nMeasure each boundary. A useful boundary reduces startup JavaScript or hydration\nwork without making expected interactions feel late.\n\n## Comparison To Astro Islands\n\nAstro starts static and asks \"what should come alive?\" Each answer is an\nisolated framework root dropped into HTML. Islands are independent runtimes\nsharing a DOM.\n\nTanStack Start starts fully interactive and asks \"what can wait?\" The whole\ndocument hydrates as one Solid tree by default; `Hydrate` boundaries are gates\ninside that tree. Context, state, and events flow through normally, and\nhydration is parent-first.\n\nSame trigger vocabulary, different substrate: Astro composes runtimes, Start\nschedules one. That is why Start gets `interaction()`, `condition()`, and intent\nbubbling, and why Astro gets multi-framework.\n\n## Comparison To Solid Streaming Hydration\n\nReact's selective hydration controls the order in which server-rendered\nboundaries hydrate. Deferred hydration controls whether and when each\nboundary hydrates at all.\n\nWhen React hydrates a streaming SSR page, every server-rendered\n`<Suspense>` boundary will eventually hydrate. Selective hydration just\ndecides the order: each boundary hydrates as soon as its code arrives,\nand React jumps a boundary to the front of the queue if the user clicks\ninside it. The work is fixed by what the server rendered; React\nschedules it to feel responsive.\n\nDeferred hydration changes what is in the queue in the first place. A\n`Hydrate` boundary names a condition — `visible()`, `idle()`,\n`interaction()`, `media()`, `condition()`, or `never()` — and the\nboundary stays as static server HTML until that condition fires. By\ndefault the child JavaScript also moves into a separate chunk that the\nbrowser does not download until the boundary is about to hydrate. If the\ncondition never fires, the boundary never hydrates and its code is never\nfetched.\n\nThe two compose. A `Hydrate` boundary decides whether and when React\nstarts hydrating a subtree; once it opens, anything inside it (including\n`<Suspense>` boundaries) flows back into React's normal hydration\nscheduler. Use `<Suspense>` when hydration must happen and you want React\nto prioritize it well. Use `Hydrate` when hydration might not need to\nhappen at all.\n\n## The Three Decisions\n\nEach `Hydrate` boundary has three performance decisions:\n\n| Decision    | Option     | What it controls                                                   |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Hydration   | `when`     | When the preserved server HTML becomes interactive.                |\n| Code split  | `split`    | Whether the children move into a generated deferred child chunk.   |\n| Preparation | `prefetch` | Whether work starts before the `when` strategy hydrates the child. |\n\n### `when`: decide when the boundary hydrates\n\n`when` is required. Pass a strategy object for the common case:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate when={visible()}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nPass a function when the decision needs browser-only information:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function RecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={() =>\n        navigator.connection?.saveData\n          ? interaction({ events: 'click' })\n          : visible()\n      }\n    >\n      <Recommendations />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe function form is evaluated only on the client and must synchronously return\na strategy. Use `never()` when you intentionally want the initial server HTML to\nstay static.\n\n### `split`: decide whether to create a separate child chunk\n\nBy default, `Hydrate` splits the children into a generated child chunk:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate when={visible()}>\n  <HeavyWidget />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nThis delays both hydration work and child JavaScript loading.\n\nSet `split={false}` when the child code is small or already needed elsewhere,\nand you only want to delay hydration work:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function SmallWidgetBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()} split={false}>\n      <SmallWidget />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### `prefetch`: decide whether to start loading before hydration\n\n`prefetch` starts loading before the boundary hydrates. It has two forms:\n\n| Form                | Example                             | Use it for                                                     |\n| ------------------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Prefetch strategy   | `prefetch={idle()}`                 | Preloading the generated child chunk before hydration.         |\n| Procedural prefetch | `prefetch={async (ctx) => { ... }}` | Preloading the child chunk plus data or other async resources. |\n\nBoth forms start work early, but they do not change when the boundary becomes\ninteractive. That is still controlled by `when`.\n\nA prefetch strategy is the small, declarative form:\n\n```tsx\nimport { idle, interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction()} prefetch={idle()}>\n  <ProductRecommendations />\n</Hydrate>\n\n<Hydrate\n  when={interaction()}\n  prefetch={visible({ rootMargin: '1200px' })}\n>\n  <RelatedProducts />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nStrategy-form `prefetch` downloads the generated child chunk before the boundary\nhydrates. This can make the later hydration trigger feel faster, because the\nbrowser may already have the chunk by the time `when` resolves. Generated child\nchunks only exist when `split` is enabled, so TypeScript rejects strategy-form\n`prefetch` when `split={false}`.\n\nUse procedural prefetch when you need custom work:\n\n```tsx\nimport { noop, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nfunction DeferredReviews() {\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient()\n\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={visible()}\n      prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n        await Promise.all([\n          preload(),\n          queryClient.query(reviewsQueryOptions).catch(noop),\n        ])\n      }}\n    >\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nProcedural prefetch also works with `split={false}`. In that case, `preload()`\nis a resolved no-op, but the function can still prepare data or other\nresources.\n\n## Common Recipes\n\n### Hydrate below-the-fold SSR content\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ProductHero />\n      <BuyBox />\n\n      <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '800px' })}>\n        <Reviews />\n      </Hydrate>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nUse a positive `rootMargin` when the boundary should hydrate before it actually\nenters the viewport.\n\n### Download the child chunk before it is needed\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ReviewsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '200px' })} prefetch={idle()}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps the boundary non-interactive until it is close to the viewport, but\nstarts loading the child chunk during idle time.\n\n### Keep a widget cold until user intent\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function RecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}\n      prefetch={visible({ rootMargin: '1200px' })}\n    >\n      <RecommendationCarousel />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThis is useful for expensive controls that are visible or nearby, but only\nmatter when the user reaches for them.\n\n### Delay hydration without code splitting\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { idle } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function BadgeBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()} split={false}>\n      <SmallPersonalizedBadge />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nUse this when the JavaScript is already part of the startup bundle or when a\nseparate child chunk would not be worth it.\n\n### Keep initial SSR HTML static\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { never } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function MarketingPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={never()}>\n      <StaticTrustBadges />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`never()` preserves the existing server HTML and does not hydrate the boundary\nduring initial document hydration. If the same boundary mounts later during\nclient-side navigation, it renders normally because there is no initial server\nHTML to preserve. `never()` cannot be used as a prefetch strategy.\n\n### Reuse Hydrate props\n\nUse `HydrateOptions` for reusable objects that you spread into `Hydrate`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport type { HydrateOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nconst belowFoldProps = {\n  when: () => visible({ rootMargin: '800px' }),\n} satisfies HydrateOptions\n\nexport function Page() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate\n      {...belowFoldProps}\n      prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n        await preload()\n      }}\n    >\n      <Widget />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nInline `when` and `prefetch` functions are supported. You do not need to wrap\nthem in `useCallback`; TanStack Start keeps the latest callback internally and\ndoes not re-register hydration listeners just because a function identity\nchanged. If the meaning of a boundary changes, use a normal React `key` to\ncreate a new boundary.\n\n## Hydrate Props Reference\n\n`Hydrate` accepts these props:\n\n| Prop         | Type                                                     | Notes                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `when`       | `HydrationStrategy \\| () => HydrationStrategy`           | Required. Controls when the boundary hydrates. Function form is client-only and synchronous.                                                              |\n| `prefetch`   | `HydrationPrefetchStrategy \\| HydrationPrefetchFunction` | Optional. Strategy form preloads the split child chunk. Function form can preload chunks, data, or other resources, and can be used with `split={false}`. |\n| `split`      | `boolean`                                                | Defaults to `true`. Set literal `false` to disable compiler extraction and only defer hydration work.                                                     |\n| `fallback`   | `JSX.Element`                                              | Client-only loading UI for boundaries that mount after the app has already hydrated and then suspend on the child chunk or child `Suspense`.              |\n| `onHydrated` | `() => void`                                             | Fires once after the boundary has hydrated on the client.                                                                                                 |\n\n## Strategy Reference\n\nImport strategies from `@tanstack/solid-start/hydration`.\n\n| Strategy        | Behavior                                                                                   |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `load()`        | Hydrates as soon as the app hydrates.                                                      |\n| `idle()`        | Hydrates in `requestIdleCallback`, or after `timeout` when idle callbacks are unavailable. |\n| `visible()`     | Hydrates when the boundary marker enters the viewport.                                     |\n| `media()`       | Hydrates when the media query matches.                                                     |\n| `interaction()` | Hydrates on configured interaction intent events.                                          |\n| `condition()`   | Hydrates once the condition is truthy.                                                     |\n| `never()`       | Never hydrates the initial server-rendered boundary.                                       |\n\nStrategy options:\n\n| Strategy      | Options                                                                                 |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `idle`        | `{ timeout?: number }`, defaults to `2000`.                                             |\n| `visible`     | `{ rootMargin?: string; threshold?: number \\| Array<number> }`, default margin `600px`. |\n| `media`       | Query string, for example `media('(min-width: 800px)')`.                                |\n| `interaction` | `{ events?: supported event or readonly array of supported events }`.                   |\n| `condition`   | Boolean or boolean-returning function.                                                  |\n\nSupported interaction events are `auxclick`, `click`, `contextmenu`,\n`dblclick`, `focusin`, `keydown`, `keyup`, `mousedown`, `mouseenter`,\n`mouseover`, `mouseup`, `pointerdown`, `pointerenter`, `pointerover`, and\n`pointerup`.\n\nThe default `interaction()` event list is `pointerenter`, `focusin`,\n`pointerdown`, and `click`. Use `events` when a boundary should listen to a\ndifferent event or a smaller set:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'dblclick' })}>\n  <PreviewEditor />\n</Hydrate>\n\n<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['contextmenu', 'dblclick'] })}>\n  <ContextMenuEditor />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nAfter a `condition()` boundary hydrates, it stays hydrated even if the condition\nlater becomes false:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { condition } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function CartRecommendationsBoundary() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={condition(isCartOpen)}>\n      <CartRecommendations />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Prefetch Reference\n\nProcedural prefetch receives a context object:\n\n| Property            | Meaning                                                                                 |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `preload()`         | Loads the compiler-generated child chunk. It resolves immediately when `split={false}`. |\n| `waitFor(strategy)` | Waits for a prefetch strategy, the hydration trigger, or abort.                         |\n| `signal`            | `AbortSignal` for cancelable async work such as `fetch`.                                |\n| `element`           | Boundary marker element for custom observers or DOM measurements.                       |\n\n`waitFor(strategy)` resolves with:\n\n| Result       | Meaning                                                             |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `'prefetch'` | The supplied prefetch strategy resolved normally.                   |\n| `'hydrate'`  | The boundary's hydration trigger fired first. Do required work now. |\n| `'abort'`    | The boundary unmounted or the prefetch lifecycle was abandoned.     |\n\nThe promise returned from procedural prefetch is meaningful. Awaited work blocks\nhydration if the `when` strategy resolves before the prefetch function\nfinishes:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate\n  when={visible()}\n  prefetch={async ({ preload }) => {\n    await preload()\n  }}\n>\n  <Widget />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nFire-and-forget work does not block hydration:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate\n  when={visible()}\n  prefetch={({ preload }) => {\n    void preload()\n  }}\n>\n  <Widget />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nUse this distinction deliberately. Await when the resource is required for the\nfirst hydrated render. Fire and forget when the resource is only a helpful\nhead start.\n\n## Fallbacks\n\n`fallback` is not the placeholder for the initial server-rendered HTML. On the\ninitial page load, TanStack Start keeps the existing server HTML in place until\nthe boundary hydrates:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate when={visible()} fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nIn that example, if `Reviews` was present in the initial HTML document, users\nsee the server-rendered reviews. They do not see `ReviewsSkeleton` while the\nboundary is waiting for `visible()`.\n\n`fallback` is used when the boundary first appears after the app is already\nrunning and there is no existing server HTML for that boundary. Common examples\ninclude client-side navigation, conditionally showing a panel, or opening a tab\nwhose contents were not in the initial document. In those cases, the boundary\nrenders on the client, and `fallback` can show while the generated child chunk\nor a child `Suspense` is still loading.\n\nWith `never()`, initial server HTML remains static and `fallback` is not used.\n\nThe compiler removes statically visible `fallback` props from the server bundle.\nPrefer passing `fallback` directly, in an inline object spread, or through a\nsingle-use `const` object spread so server builds can strip that UI.\n\n## Correctness And Updates\n\nDeferred hydration is a performance hint for React's initial hydration work.\nReact may hydrate a deferred boundary earlier than its strategy would normally\nallow if state, props, context, or store updates outside the boundary require\nReact to reconcile inside it before the gate opens. This preserves correctness\nand avoids showing stale server HTML after the surrounding app has changed.\n\n`never()` is the exception for initial document hydration. Treat it as\nintentionally static SSR HTML. Do not rely on parent updates to make a `never()`\nboundary interactive. If the same boundary mounts later during client-side\nnavigation, it renders normally.\n\n## Nested Boundaries\n\nNested boundaries hydrate parent-first. A child boundary can only hydrate after\nits ancestor boundaries have hydrated. That means non-interaction child\nstrategies such as `visible`, `media`, `idle`, or `condition` cannot run while\ntheir parent boundary is still dehydrated.\n\nFor example, a product page might defer the whole reviews section until it is\nnear the viewport, while keeping heavier review tools cold until the user\ninteracts with them:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\nimport { interaction, visible } from '@tanstack/solid-start/hydration'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <>\n      <ProductHero />\n      <BuyBox />\n\n      <Hydrate when={visible({ rootMargin: '600px' })}>\n        <section aria-labelledby=\"reviews-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"reviews-heading\">Reviews</h2>\n          <ReviewsSummary />\n          <ReviewsList />\n\n          <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}>\n            <ReviewFilters />\n          </Hydrate>\n\n          <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'click' })}>\n            <WriteReviewForm />\n          </Hydrate>\n        </section>\n      </Hydrate>\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nIn this example, scrolling near the reviews hydrates the parent first. Only\nafter that can the nested interaction boundaries hydrate from focus or click.\n\nInteraction intent can also resolve an unresolved ancestor chain when the\nancestor is itself waiting for interaction:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate when={interaction({ events: ['focusin', 'click'] })}>\n  <section aria-label=\"Review tools\">\n    <ReviewSortSummary />\n\n    <Hydrate when={interaction({ events: 'click' })}>\n      <WriteReviewForm />\n    </Hydrate>\n  </section>\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nIf the first meaningful intent is a click inside `WriteReviewForm`, TanStack\nStart hydrates the unresolved parent chain and then redispatches a same-type\nevent for the target boundary. Native listener payload details such as pointer\ncoordinates are not guaranteed to be preserved. A `never()` ancestor still wins\nduring initial hydration, so descendants under it remain non-interactive.\n\n## Preloading And CSS\n\nTransformed `Hydrate` JavaScript chunks are not modulepreloaded with the route.\nWithout `prefetch`, the child chunk loads when the split boundary is ready to\nrender. If that import suspends during client-side navigation or another\nclient-only mount, the boundary's `fallback` is shown.\n\nCSS used by split, deferred, and `never()` boundaries is linked in the SSR HTML\nfor the matched route. It is not deferred with the generated child JavaScript\nchunk, because the server-rendered HTML may need those styles before any\nJavaScript runs. This is route-level asset linking: if a route module contains a\ndeferred boundary that imports CSS, that stylesheet can be linked for the route\neven when that boundary is hidden behind conditional rendering and does not\nappear in a particular response.\n\n## Extraction Limits\n\nCompiler-backed `Hydrate` splitting works by moving the boundary's children into\na generated virtual module and rendering them through a lazy component. That\ngives TanStack Start a separate child chunk to load later, but it also means the\ncompiler must be able to move the JSX safely.\n\nKeep the component you want to split directly inside `Hydrate`. If you hide it\nbehind opaque `children` props, the compiler cannot statically extract those\nchildren into a generated child chunk at the usage site.\n\nThe split boundary must use a statically imported `Hydrate` component from\n`@tanstack/solid-start`. Renaming that import is supported:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate as Deferred } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Deferred when={visible()}>\n      <Reviews />\n    </Deferred>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nAssigning `Hydrate` to another component variable is not analyzed for splitting:\n\n```tsx\nimport { Hydrate } from '@tanstack/solid-start'\n\nconst Deferred = Hydrate\n\n<Deferred when={visible()}>\n  <Reviews />\n</Deferred>\n```\n\nRender the imported `Hydrate` tag directly, use an import rename, or set\n`split={false}` when you need component indirection.\n\nUse the literal prop `split={false}` to opt out of extraction. Dynamic values\nsuch as `split={shouldSplit}` cannot be used to opt out at compile time.\n\nThese patterns cannot be split:\n\n| Pattern                                  | Why it is rejected                                                                 | What to do instead                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Function-as-children                     | The compiler cannot move a render function and preserve the expected call pattern. | Use `split={false}` or move the rendered UI into a child component.                  |\n| Render-time `use*` calls directly inside extracted JSX | Moving that JSX would move where the call executes.                                | Move the call into a component inside the boundary, then render that component. |\n| `this` captures                          | Extracted function components cannot safely preserve class instance context.       | Wrap the UI in a function component or use `split={false}`.                          |\n| `super` captures                         | Extracted function components cannot preserve superclass access.                   | Wrap the UI in a function component or use `split={false}`.                          |\n\nThis fails because `useThing()` would be moved into the generated component:\n\n```tsx\n<Hydrate when={idle()}>\n  <p>{useThing()}</p>\n</Hydrate>\n```\n\nMove the call into a component instead:\n\n```tsx\nfunction ThingText() {\n  const thing = useThing()\n  return <p>{thing}</p>\n}\n\nexport function ProductPage() {\n  return (\n    <Hydrate when={idle()}>\n      <ThingText />\n    </Hydrate>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nValues captured from the surrounding component can be passed into the generated\nchild component, but keep the boundary simple. If extraction starts forcing\ncomplicated data flow, prefer a named child component and put the logic there.\n\n`fallback` stripping is intentionally conservative. The server build can strip\ndirectly passed fallback UI, inline object-spread fallback UI, and single-use\n`const` object-spread fallback UI. If fallback props are hidden behind dynamic\nspreads or shared objects, the compiler may keep them.\n\nYou can extract reusable `when` and `prefetch` helpers today, but avoid hiding\nsplit boundaries behind plain wrapper components if you need child code\nsplitting. A wrapper can defer hydration at runtime, but the compiler cannot\nreliably move call-site children into a separate chunk through arbitrary\ncomponent indirection.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nref: docs/start/framework/react/guide/deferred-hydration.md\nreplace:\n  '@tanstack/react-start': '@tanstack/solid-start'\n  'React handlers': 'Solid handlers'\n  'one React tree': 'one Solid tree'\n  'Comparison To React Selective Hydration': 'Comparison To Solid Streaming Hydration'\n  \"React's selective hydration controls the order in which server-rendered boundaries hydrate. Deferred hydration controls whether and when each boundary hydrates at all.\": \"Solid's streaming hydration controls the order in which server-rendered boundaries hydrate. Deferred hydration controls whether and when each boundary hydrates at all.\"\n  'When React hydrates a streaming SSR page, every server-rendered `<Suspense>` boundary will eventually hydrate. Selective hydration just decides the order: each boundary hydrates as soon as its code arrives, and React jumps a boundary to the front of the queue if the user clicks inside it. The work is fixed by what the server rendered; React schedules it to feel responsive.': 'When Solid hydrates a streaming SSR page, every server-rendered `<Suspense>` boundary will eventually hydrate. Streaming hydration just decides the order: each boundary hydrates as its resources resolve and stream from the server. The work is fixed by what the server rendered; Solid streams it to feel responsive.'\n  \"The two compose. A `Hydrate` boundary decides whether and when React starts hydrating a subtree; once it opens, anything inside it (including `<Suspense>` boundaries) flows back into React's normal hydration scheduler. Use `<Suspense>` when hydration must happen and you want React to prioritize it well. Use `Hydrate` when hydration might not need to happen at all.\": \"The two compose. A `Hydrate` boundary decides whether and when Solid starts hydrating a subtree; once it opens, anything inside it (including `<Suspense>` boundaries) flows back into Solid's normal hydration scheduler. Use `<Suspense>` when hydration must happen and you want Solid to prioritize it well. Use `Hydrate` when hydration might not need to happen at all.\"\n  'ReactNode': 'JSX.Element'\n  \"Deferred hydration is a performance hint for React's initial hydration work. React may hydrate a deferred boundary earlier than its strategy would normally allow if state, props, context, or store updates outside the boundary require React to reconcile inside it before the gate opens. This preserves correctness and avoids showing stale server HTML after the surrounding app has changed.\": \"Deferred hydration is a performance hint for Solid's initial hydration work. Once a boundary gate opens, TanStack Start clears the preserved server DOM inside the marker and mounts the live Solid subtree in its place.\"\n  'Hook calls directly inside extracted JSX': 'Render-time `use*` calls directly inside extracted JSX'\n  'Moving that JSX would move where the hook executes.': 'Moving that JSX would move where the call executes.'\n  'Move the hook call into a component inside the boundary, then render that component.': 'Move the call into a component inside the boundary, then render that component.'\n  'Move the hook into a component instead:': 'Move the call into a component instead:'\n---\n"}
